---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { WORK_WITH_ME_PATH } from '../consts';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="14 years of enterprise software experience, now expanding into AI/ML and business automation. What I've built, and what I haven't."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-24">
    <span class="label-mono text-xs text-(--color-accent)">About</span>
    <h1 class="font-display mb-8 mt-3 text-4xl font-semibold text-(--color-ink)">
      What I've actually built, and where I haven't.
    </h1>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        I'm John DeLeon. 14 years in enterprise software, most of it in the insurance industry,
        writing C# microservices for carrier and web integrations &mdash; promoted from developer
        to Lead Software Developer to Software Engineer along the way. For 5 of those years I was
        the Java technical lead directing an event-driven claims-system implementation alongside
        the software provider.
      </p>
      <p>
        I finished an MS in Computer Science at Angelo State University in December 2025, with an
        ML focus and Python coursework. That degree, not a bootcamp or a weekend course, is where
        the AI/ML side of this started.
      </p>

      <hr class="my-12 border-(--color-border)" />

      <h2 class="font-display mb-4 text-2xl font-semibold text-(--color-ink)">The throughline</h2>
      <p>
        14 years of enterprise experience, now deliberately expanding into AI and business
        automation. Not a pivot away from what I know &mdash; an extension of it. That's what this
        site is: the record of that extension, including the parts that are still unresolved.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-display mb-4 mt-12 text-2xl font-semibold text-(--color-ink)">
        What I've built
      </h2>
      <ul class="space-y-4 pl-5 list-disc my-6">
        <li>
          <strong>A DOD-funded capstone</strong> &mdash; a Kafka/Spark/Neo4j/TimescaleDB pipeline
          training graph neural network models for anomaly detection with explainability, run
          against a real IEEE Dataport hardware-in-the-loop testbed dataset. This was a class
          project, not a production deployment.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>A fraud detector for job postings</strong> &mdash; text classification with a
          full backend/frontend and an AWS CDK deployment around it. Side project, built to see the
          whole pipeline through, not just the model.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>A production ordering site</strong> for a real cottage-food bakery (Astro,
          Supabase, Cloudflare) &mdash; I directed an AI-assisted build with Claude Code, meaning I
          prompted, reviewed, and evaluated its output rather than hand-writing every line, and
          configured the self-hosted n8n automation behind it. This one is live and in use, not a
          demo.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="font-display mb-4 mt-12 text-2xl font-semibold text-(--color-ink)">
        What I don't have standing on
      </h2>
      <p>
        Two things I won't pretend expertise in just because I touch them:
      </p>
      <ul class="space-y-3 pl-5 list-disc my-6">
        <li>
          <strong>Performance engineering and security.</strong> I think about them when I build.
          I don't have deep expertise in either, and I won't write like I do.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Frontend design.</strong> I'm mid at best. I lean on AI tooling to do the actual
          design work, and I'll say so when it's relevant.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <hr class="my-12 border-(--color-border)" />

      <p>
        If you want the build logs, they're on the <a href="/blog/">blog</a>. If you're evaluating
        whether to hire me for automation or AI-integration work, that's a separate conversation
        &mdash; see <a href={WORK_WITH_ME_PATH}>what I work on</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
